Nothing on the clipboard is a save folder (a folder with an icon.sys).
Unpack PSU here
Cross opens a folder, or shows what can be done with a file. Square marks it. Triangle shows what can be done with it. L1/R1 turn the page, Circle goes up a folder.
Copies or moves what is on the clipboard into this folder. A name already here is never replaced: it is skipped and named. A save folder pasted onto a memory card goes in the card's root, and a .psu pasted onto one unpacks into its save.
Makes a folder here, with a name you type.
Puts the marked entries, or this one if none are marked, on the clipboard. Paste here copies them.
Puts the marked entries, or this one if none are marked, on the clipboard. Paste here moves them; each one leaves its old place only once it is whole in the new one.
Gives this entry a new name, typed on the keyboard.
Deletes the marked entries, or this one if none are marked, folders with everything in them. You are asked first.
Makes one .psu file here from each save folder on the clipboard (a folder with an icon.sys): the save file uLaunchELF, EMS and Apollo use. The saves themselves are not changed.
Unpacks this .psu into its save folder here. On a memory card the save goes in the card's root, where games look for it.
Opens this folder.
Starts this ELF, the way an app on the Apps page starts.
Marks this entry, so Copy, Cut and Delete act on every marked one. Square on a row does the same.
